**How to implement.** The window names every new setup by the kit's naming template (001 §J 'It names setups and experiments'; S8.2 interpretation 8: a table that is no setup yet takes `Setup <n>` at a commit or a swap, a swap from an active setup `<name> (2)`, and 'S8.3's template replaces these names'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, which opens `NamingTemplates`: (1) `ExpCommit` on a table that is no setup yet (step 261 (8)(b)): the setup is `Setup.create name slots model.kitSetups` with `name` = `model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate.setupNameAmong slots model.kitItems taken (SetupName.firstFree taken)` (step 271), `taken` being the names of `kitSetups` and `slots` the recorded table step 261 builds; `nextFreeAmong` keeps the name free, so `create` refuses none. (2) `SwapSlot` (step 264): the fresh name of a `CreateSwappedSetup` is `setupNameAmong swapped model.kitItems taken <step 264's fresh name>`, so a swapped table the template names takes that name and one it cannot name keeps `<active> (2)` or `Setup <n>`. (3) Nothing else is named here: `CreateSetup` keeps the typed name (step 260), and a copied setup keeps its own (step 261). The template is read from the kit file the window holds (`KitContext.kitFile`, step 131), so a template saved in the window names the next setup (step 273). No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (steps 260, 263, 264), whose kit holds step 263's items `LP1`, `QZ`, `Laser` and `LPd` and step 264's `QZ2`, and whose kit file holds `NamingTemplate.standard`: `a commit on a table the kit's template names records it under that name`: with a linear polarizer, a sample and a second linear polarizer added, as step 263's facts add elements, so that the light meets them in that order before the seeded detector; `LP1` assigned to the first, `QZ` to the sample, turned to R1 45° (`RotSetAxis (R1, BarDegrees 45.0)` with it selected), and `LPd` to the second, each by `AssignSlot` (step 263); the first polarizer chosen (`ExpChooseElement`) and `ExpCommit`: the kit holds `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.setup-json` at revision 1, `E1` references it, and `activeSetupOpt` is that setup. `a swap to content no setup holds takes the template's name of the swapped table`: after that commit, `SwapSlot (sample, QZ2)` writes `LP1-(QZ2#45)-LPd.setup-json`, makes it active, and leaves the bytes of `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.setup-json` unchanged. Step 261's and 264's facts keep their names (`Setup 1`, `Bench A (2)`), and so do the UI facts that find `Setup 1.setup-json` (step 261): their tables hold no item in Prep 1, Obj 1 or Analyzer 1, which `NamingTemplate.standard` requires (step 268).

**Acceptance.** After the window names new setups by the template, a commit on a table that is no setup yet and a swap to content no setup holds MUST name the new setup by the kit's naming template made free, and keep S8.2's name for a table the template cannot name; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a commit on a table the kit's template names records it under that name` and `a swap to content no setup holds takes the template's name of the swapped table`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.
